    "q-91337": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91337",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find all of the real solutions to the equation ${x}^{6}=64.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by taking the $6$th root of each side and solving for $x.$ Since the exponent $(6)$  is even, we consider both the positive and negative solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{6} & =64 \\\\ \\sqrt[6]{{x}^{6}} & =\\pm \\sqrt[6]{64} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt[6]{{2}^{6}} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
