    "q-111442": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111442",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find all of the real solutions to the equation $\\frac{(x+4)^{4}}{25}=25.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by isolating the $(x+4)^{4}$ term and then taking the $4$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $(x+4)^{4}$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{4}}{25} & =25 \\\\ (x+4)^{4} & =625\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $4$th root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since the exponent $(4)$ is even, we consider both the positive and negative solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{4} & =625 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{(x+4)^{4}} & =\\pm \\sqrt[4]{625} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm \\sqrt[4]{{5}^{4}} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-9$ and $x=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-111442-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "There are no real solutions",
              "html": "There are no real solutions"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-111442-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$5$ only",
